{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"40112892-37a2-494f-a55b-08dd7f5dcbf0","runId":"af1691fa-2cad-4207-a064-a8d95ad2be35","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":9,"previousEventHash":"sha256:8dbee7b34c6f774aab40eaf03365d9357fcb2374c50893257ebc864f3041c96d","type":"node.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a037ea-6d15-724a-8efc-8c2eebdfc4d2","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-25T08:08:23.378Z","idempotencyKey":"node:investigate-1:completed","payload":{"nodeId":"investigate-1","node":"investigate","attempt":1,"round":1,"headSha":"4819168331da2a25f500a1d1436f231db8211f2b","baseSha":"4819168331da2a25f500a1d1436f231db8211f2b","outcome":"confirmed","verificationResults":[],"evidence":["Issue #14 identifies SEC-ISSUE1-004 from PR #6 and requests symlink-race hardening, local-attacker documentation, and focused replacement tests.","The frozen base predates PR #6 hardening: src/agents/runtime-paths.ts is absent and commit 1e2a635ff05080dda36c17efe409e86af4fe17c4 is not an ancestor of the frozen HEAD.","src/agents/materialize.ts:27 recursively creates .pi/agents without checking existing path components; lines 100 and 129-151 use path-based writeFile calls for agent definitions, settings, and generated-settings.","A temporary Linux reproduction with .pi symlinked to an external directory caused materializeForgeAgents to create agents, forge/generated-settings, and settings.json in that external target, demonstrating symlink following; temporary data was removed and the assigned worktree remained clean.","src/adapters/git.ts:63-90 reads and appends .git/info/exclude by path without no-follow or directory-handle protection, so a local replacement of the file or parent can redirect the authority-sensitive append.","Existing tests cover ordinary materialization in test/adapters/subagents.test.ts and ordinary Git exclude handling in test/adapters/git.test.ts, but no symlink replacement coverage exists.","The current Linux Node environment exposes O_NOFOLLOW and O_DIRECTORY; the package supports Node >=22 and must handle unavailable platform primitives explicitly rather than using an unsafe path-based fallback."]}}
